{"id":242,"slug":"taste-of-cherry","title":"Taste of Cherry","year":1997,"country":"Iran","duration":99,"spine":45,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/242-taste-of-cherry","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/2b3cb1e242f75f984a61305a512a8417/0IZ7RI0ApmwUqfotR9mOZmFlhsHjvo_large.jpg","description":"The first Iranian film to win the Palme d’Or, this austere, emotionally complex drama by the greatAbbas Kiarostami follows the enigmatic Mr. Badii (Homayoun Ershadi) as he drives around the hilly outskirts of Tehran looking for someone who will agree to bury him after he commits suicide, a taboo under Islam. Extended conversations with three passengers (a soldier, a seminarian, and a taxidermist) elicit different views on mortality and individual choice. Operating at once as a closely observed, realistic story and a fable populated by archetypal figures, Taste of Cherry challenges the viewer to consider what often goes unexamined in everyday life.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Abbas Kiarostami","slug":"abbas-kiarostami"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Homayoun Ershadi","role":"Mr. Badii","slug":"homayoun-ershadi"},{"actor":"Abdol Hossein Bagheri","role":"Taxidermist","slug":"abdol-hossein-bagheri"},{"actor":"Afshin Khorshid Bakhtiari","role":"Worker","slug":"afshin-khorshid-bakhtiari"},{"actor":"Safar Ali Moradi","role":"Soldier","slug":"safar-ali-moradi"},{"actor":"Mir Hossein Noori","role":"Seminarist","slug":"mir-hossein-noori"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Abbas Kiarostami","slug":"abbas-kiarostami"},{"role":"Written and produced by","person":"Abbas Kiarostami","slug":"abbas-kiarostami"},{"role":"Cinematography","person":"Homayoun Payvar","slug":null},{"role":"Sound","person":"Jahangir Mirshekari","slug":null},{"role":"Mix","person":"Mohammad Reza Delpak","slug":null},{"role":"First assistant director","person":"Hassan Yektapanah","slug":null},{"role":"Second assistant director","person":"Bahman Kiarostami","slug":null}],"pick